// Title: File Download And Execution Via IEExec.EXE
// Sigma ID: 9801abb8-e297-4dbf-9fbd-57dde0e830ad
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-05-16 | Modified: 2023-11-09
// ATT&CK: command-and-control, T1105
// Description: Detects execution of the IEExec utility to download and execute files
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/Ieexec/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_ieexec_download.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\IEExec.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "IEExec.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "http://" or ProcessCommandLine contains "https://")
